The new ARM environment qualifies all 187 benchmark-designated checks for `psf__requests-6028`: the unfixed source passes 185 and fails the two required failing checks; the gold source passes all 187. The unchanged native SWE-bench 5.0.2 grader resolves only the gold control. **Both collected outputs also contain eight missing-fixture setup errors outside the designated set.** This is designated-check environment qualification, not an error-free full-suite result, fresh model result or trajectory enrollment.

| Control | Designated checks completed | Designated passes | Required failing checks still failing | Native resolved |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Unfixed source | 187/187 | 185 | 2/2 | No |
| Gold source | 187/187 | 187 | 0/2 | Yes |

Neither control has a missing, skipped or errored designated check. Neither times out or is killed for memory. Their execution times were 2.17 and 2.32 seconds. The original evaluation script has no test-exit-code marker and returns container status 0 for both controls; success therefore requires nonempty, complete designated result evidence and the native grade, not the shell exit status alone. The eight other setup errors are visibly retained in `nonexpected_error_triage.json` and the count summaries. No hidden test IDs, fixture names, patch contents, task text or raw logs were exposed to agent context.

This is an explicit ARM port of the published x86 environment. It uses the immutable ARM Python 3.9.20 base `sha256:5772df931ea2bad11e17170ce221f86c751c91eaa537733f069e20bbbb8e9fa7`, preserves all 13 Python package versions listed in the official public environment, and substitutes the Debian ARM system stack for the x86 conda/system packages. The resulting image is `sha256:286803e9de8b76e7299a7905e684841182ecac54ce55378f4ba1a92a1f497bcd`. The full recipe, explicit original-to-port diff and installed Python/system package versions are retained. No equivalence to the published x86 image is claimed.

The source is checked out at the exact base commit `0192aac24123735b3eaf9b08df46429bb770c283`. Curator code confirmed that the pinned dataset and task repository have byte-identical gold patches, test patches and evaluation scripts, and identical designated test sets. Those protected values were processed only within custody; public outputs contain hashes and counts. The original script was retained verbatim except for four exact conda activation lines. Its actual hidden test commands and test patch remain unchanged. Evaluation containers have no network, two CPUs, a 2 GiB memory limit and a 128-process limit.

The final scorer uses ordinary imports of the actual upstream package and initializer in a dedicated local virtual environment. The missing real Docker SDK, unidiff, Modal and datasets dependencies were installed there; all 545 available distribution versions and 27 loaded upstream source modules are recorded. An initially drafted initializer-bypass loader was never executed and is not part of the admitted profile. Initial ordinary-import failures are preserved.

The first unfixed execution produced non-UTF-8 bytes, and a strict text read failed. Its original raw bytes, process status and exception are retained. A separately frozen v2 scorer applies the exact upstream `docker_utils.py` decoding behavior, `decode(errors="replace")`, before invoking the unchanged parser. It reuses that already executed unfixed control and separately executes gold. Raw bytes, decoded bytes, hashes and replacement counts are all retained in custody; no execution results were silently replaced. There were two actual control executions in total. An initial audit incorrectly compared universal-newline text with raw decoded text; that failed audit is retained, and the final audit compares the exact output bytes.

The final read-only audit passed 180 checks covering input/source identities, ordinary native imports, original task/dataset custody, exact script adaptation, installed versions, raw/decoded log identity, nonempty complete designated results, control direction and absence of hidden test IDs or patch payloads in sanitized artifacts. It makes no new scoring or provider calls. Native scorer adversarial integrity, error-free full-suite execution, historical trajectory compatibility and model enrollment remain separate qualifications.

Results are under `run-v1/scoring-v2/score_summary.json`; source/environment bindings are in `run-v1/freeze.json` and `run-v1/scoring-v2/native_scorer_freeze.json`; the audit is `run-v1/artifact_audit.json`. `service_contract.json` exposes the public qualification identity and describes the custody boundary for a future candidate adapter. Raw custody stays under a directory with mode 0700. All temporary qualification containers were removed; the 93.4 MB image and approximately 65 MiB of local artifacts/environment remain. Zero provider calls or tokens were used.
